Luca Pacioli (1445–1517) discussed the construction of the regular polygons in his *De divina proportione*, entitled for his term for the extreme and mean ratio. In the preceding diagram, the 12 vertices of icosahedron appear in three groups of four vertices, each group being the vertices of three mutually perpendicular rectangles, *LMTU*, *OXRZ*, and *NPSQ*.

Pacioli recognized that the sides of each of those rectangles are in extreme and mean ratio, and used them as the construction of the icosahedron.

#### Use of this construction

Constructing a icosahedron is an end in itself. This construction and the corollary are also used in @XIII.18 where the five regular polyhedra are compared.
